      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You've hit on a crucial tension: while restorative justice better aligns with progressive values of bias reduction and systemic healing, many legal scholars argue that eliminating all punitive measures is currently impossible due to the entrenched nature of state power and public safety needs. Ultimately, a truly morally sound modern society would need to systematically dismantle the punitive infrastructure first, making restorative justice the sole legitimate framework once those structures no longer serve to oppress marginalized groups.",
      "source": "target",
