      "content": "that's a pretty bold claim to say restorative justice is the \"sole legitimate framework\" once those structures are gone. wouldn't people argue that there's an inherent moral necessity for some form of retribution—like, you can't have justice if there isn't a proportional consequence for a crime, regardless of the social structure? isn't that a basic human moral intuition?",
